{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792100758,"nonce":"THOR5luzSqeTl9L9K58lO5+j4fI=","message":"The AOT cache forwarding defect is confirmed independently, but it did not cause the NUC UnicodeSequences lookup failure. The actual cause was duplicate CLI manifest resolution: an absolute entry outside the project led the second resolution to drop the original class paths. Removing the outer resolution fixes that; an absolute-entry regression fails on the prior binary and compiles on the fixed one. Native execution then exposed a separate Linux allocator relocation failure, tracked in 841bc8d5614295e6cd230a77e042334d764699aae675fbfdee9a823618d3e535.","files":null}]}